        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3c696a280a8345688c453b15a0893479",
      "statement": "The dev compose stack for mc-db caps WiredTiger's cache at 1 GB and restores its sweeper defaults (wiredTigerFileHandleCloseIdleTime=30s, wiredTigerFileHandleCloseMinimum=250) because MongoDB's own default sweeper thresholds (closeIdleTime=600s, closeMinimum=2000) never became eligible for sweeping under the integration test harness's per-test database churn, driving open data-handle counts to 65,844 and causing an OOM-kill that surfaced as 'unexpected end of file'/connection-refused errors indistinguishable from a MongoDB consistency bug (item #468).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/mc-service/compose.yaml#L1-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:29b37c4bce4425b0f5d5f185dc5425b381ea5d2efd615aeda5825f0f4ae7fcfc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8e844d1069a34c6aaa477718a150aa2f",
      "statement": "The BFF owns its own MongoDB instance (`mcm-bff-db`, holding per-user agent config) that is physically separate from mc-service's `mc-db`, because no component reaches across a service boundary into another service's database; `mcm-bff-db` is a plain standalone `mongod` with no replica set and no directConnection because the BFF does single-document upserts only, unlike `mc-db` whose single-member replica set exists for mc-service's cascade-delete transaction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/MCM-Architecture.md#L142-L152",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b6e4c763866ea0dff96416f0faacbe0643abd990a334b032efc28dbce96a172:"
