    {
      "id": "claim_10c9da12199045d593f48a730a1e7e51",
      "statement": "mc-service runs Keycloak OIDC discovery and the JWKS fetch in a background task at startup, so it binds and serves immediately even when Keycloak is unreachable: /health still answers but every protected request is rejected with 401. A *failed* discovery still marks the auth instance ready, so integration tests must gate on discovery actually succeeding (is_operational) rather than on the attempt completing, otherwise the whole auth-negative suite passes green against a dead Keycloak.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/mc-service/src/api/router.rs#L144-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1bd5b689ed14bdf20c8d63172b27741cd60cc639cacdbdaa5572924847295af3:"
