    {
      "id": "claim_2724caf2623d4dd985dafb15d2818b93",
      "statement": "Feature 073's backup destination containers (the S3-compatible and WebDAV targets the integration tier tests against) live in their own compose file rather than a profile inside the `mcm` stack, because Docker Compose interpolates every service in an included file at parse time regardless of which profiles are selected — a `${REGISTRY_HOST:?}` in a profile-gated service aborted `up` for the whole `mcm` stack, including CI's app-e2e bring-up which sets no registry host. A profile is therefore not isolation from interpolation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/backups/compose.yaml#L9-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b6109dcd2ab75f94fb629115ebbf1074227f78ab395b735cd06f6bc3b12c5ea:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/mcm.compose.yaml#L15-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a67a2963fda7eb865b166f98e76de1b9785de685ccabfa16e4422fb0a55bbaa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3931d840593e40748931e80b0c146129",
      "statement": "The BFF's backup scheduler is an in-process `setInterval` in `server.js` that POSTs to `/bff-api/backups/tick` over 127.0.0.1 with the tick secret, is disabled outright (announced once at boot) when `BACKUP_TICK_SECRET` is unset, logs only when a job actually ran, and never fires under `pnpm start` because `server.js` does not run under Metro — in dev the tick route must be called directly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/backups.md#L61-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8917a10db42c8abca3b843fdd33ddd398802a2c27c64dc732bd8341c161a13ef:"
        },
